 assumes all flags precede package targets and stops scanning when it encounters a flag/value pair. For `go test`, flags like `-run` are commonly placed *after* the package list (e.g. `go test ./pkg -run TestX`), and the current reverse-scan will break at `TestX`/`-run` and return no package targets, causing callers to fall back to \".\".\n\nInstead of breaking on flags/flag-values, skip them and keep scanning earlier args so package targets are still collected regardless of ordering (while still skipping known flag values). Add a regression case for `[]string{\"./pkg\",\"-run\",\"TestX\"}` in TestSplitBuildTargets.\n```\n\t\tif i > 0 && (flagsWithPathValues[args[i-1]] || testFlagsWithValues[args[i-1]]) {\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// If we hit a flag, stop. Packages come after all flags\n```\n**tool/internal/setup/setup_test.go:146**\n* TestSplitBuildTargets covers `go test -run TestX ./pkg`, but it does not cover the common `go test ./pkg -run TestX` form where flags come after the package list. Adding that case will prevent regressions in splitBuildTargets for `go test` argument ordering.\n```\n\t\t\tname:        \"all file targets\",\n\t\t\ttargets:     []string{\"./cmd/main.go\", \"./cmd/util.go\"},\n\t\t\tpkgTargets:  nil,\n\t\t\tfileTargets: []string{\"./cmd/main.go\", \"./cmd/util.go\"},\n\t\t\texpectError: false,\n```\n</details>\n\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/562#pullrequestreview-4570552053","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/562","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/562#pullrequestreview-4570552053"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/562"}},"submitted_at":"2026-06-25T11:42:26Z","commit_id":"25bc493214d75832e44b158